-resume reloads\",\"evidence\":\"AC-1.5 requires reload reconstruction from durable state, specifically the resolved thread id (story lines 51-53). The revised resolveReloadThread handles --session by id, but for no-flag and --resume it lists threads by cwd and chooses listed.value.at(-1) at packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:118-147. The implementor artifact records that a concurrent same-cwd session could be selected instead and defers precise reload lineage to Feature 2+. The test at packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:335-370 proves only the single-thread-in-cwd case, not reconstruction from the prior resolved thread id.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.5\",\"TC-1.5\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production --resume still does not resolve an operator selection\",\"evidence\":\"AC-1.7 requires --resume/-r to list cwd-scoped threads with title and creation time and resolve the operator's selection (story lines 59-61; tech design lines 231 and 251-253). The revised defaultSelectThread shows the list via ctx.ui.notify but then returns mostRecent.threadId at packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:157-176. The production test asserts notification plus most-recent behavior at packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:255-290. The implementor artifact records this as a spec deviation because the available PI UI surface has notify but no interactive input.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.7\",\"TC-1.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-1.1 / TC-1.1: no-flag session_start creates one cwd/title registry thread and one background LHC instance; lifecycle tests and pi-lhc verify pass.\",\"AC-1.2 / TC-1.2: existing --session launch attaches to the existing thread and creates no second thread.\",\"AC-1.3 / TC-1.3 plain-data holder: connector snapshot remains structuredClone-able across fresh ctx objects.\",\"AC-1.4 / TC-1.4: shutdown dispose flush preserves pre-shutdown intake events across re-resolve.\",\"AC-1.6 / TC-1.6: launch modes and bad/ambiguous id behavior remain covered.\",\"A-8 registry support remains covered by lhc threads-a8 focused test.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-1.5 / TC-1.5 for no-flag and --resume reload reconstruction from the resolved thread id; current implementation uses cwd-most-recent registry selection.\",\"AC-1.7 / TC-1.7 production operator selection; current implementation presents choices but auto-selects most recent.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec vitest run test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter lhc exec vitest run test/threads-a8.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Reload production path for no-flag/--resume uses cwd-most-recent registry selection, not the prior resolved thread id.\",\"Production --resume presents choices through notify but auto-selects most recent; there is no real operator selection in the production path.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"needs-human-ruling\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"openQuestions\":[\"Does Lee accept cwd-most-recent registry reattach as satisfying AC-1.5 for Story 1 despite the known concurrent same-cwd limitation?\",\"Does Lee accept notify-list plus most-recent default as satisfying AC-1.7 until PI exposes an interactive selection surface?\"],\"additionalObservations\":[\"The story and epic gates pass: pi-lhc verify and verify-all both passed with 33 tests.\",\"The prior module-scope reload memory implementation is gone; the remaining SV-001 issue is the replacement behavior, not retained module state.\",\"The fail-closed observeOnlyProvider remains unchanged from the prior review and was not part of the follow-up fix surface.\"]}"}}
